{"role":"tool","content":"[subagent Extract PDF text from zip · 17 tool uses]\nI'll start by inspecting the archive and available tooling.\n\nBash appears to be blocked. Let me verify with the other tools.\n\nBash is fully blocked. Let me try the read tool on the archive and PDFs directly.\n\nBash returned a permission error. Let me confirm it's consistently blocked and check for alternatives.\n\n## (1) Result: **FAILED — I could not extract the text.**\n\n**Bash is blocked for me, explicitly.** Every `bash` call returned the identical hard error, with no interactive prompt available to approve it:\n\n```\npermission required but no prompt available for bash\n```\n\nAttempts that all failed: `cd /d \"D:\\GoatCode-ts\\gaia\" && dir data`, `where python; where pdftotext; where pip`, `echo test`, `ls`, `powershell -NoProfile -Command \"Write-Output hello\"`. There is no fallback shell, and background execution is not available either.\n\nI also cannot reach the content by any other route:\n\n| Path tried | Outcome |\n|---|---|\n| `read data/bfcd99e1-…-0174a8629083.zip` | Returns raw bytes, lossily mojibake-decoded. I can see the entry name `Job Listing.pdf`, but the body is DEFLATE-compressed and I have no decompressor. Reading the whole file to the end (461 lines) yielded only binary noise. |\n| `read` on the project's `.pdf` files | `read` does **not** parse PDFs — it dumps raw PDF source. Streams are `/FlateDecode`, i.e. unreadable without zlib. (Also note the PDF I sampled, `data/366e2f2b-…pdf`, has `/Title (SeahorseIsland)`, `/Creator (Google Sheets)` — **it is not the job listing**.) |\n| `glob` for `**/*Job*`, `tmp/**`, `extract/**` | No already-extracted copy of the PDF exists anywhere in the project. |\n| `websearch` | `permission required but no prompt available for websearch` |\n| `webfetch` | `permission required but no prompt available for webfetch` |\n| `screenshot` (to open the PDF in a viewer) | `permission required but no prompt available for computer` |\n\nI deliberately am **not** reproducing any \"job requirements\" or applicant names. Nothing in this session gave me a single legible word of the PDF's actual content, and inventing the qualifications list or applicant credentials would be worse than reporting the failure. The only verbatim strings I obtained were PDF structure (`%PDF-1.4`, `/Pages`, `/Font1`, `MUFUZY+ArialMT`, `Alpha0`) from an unrelated file.\n\n## (2) To unblock this, any one of:\n\n1. **Grant bash permission** (the cleanest fix — `Expand-Archive` + `pip install pypdf`, or `pdftotext`).\n2. **Pre-extract** `Job Listing.pdf` into the repo, e.g. `D:\\GoatCode-ts\\gaia\\data\\job-listing.pdf`, and tell me the path.\n3. **Attach a PNG/JPG render of the PDF pages** — the `read` tool does display images to me visually, so I could transcribe them verbatim.\n4. Enable `webfetch` and give me a public URL for the file.","toolCallId":"call_cedebb0064d84623971e1170","name":"task"}
